Dharna Dash: Privacy Policy
Last updated: 17 October 2026

Dharna Dash ("the game") is an offline game. This policy explains what happens to information while you play.

What we collect

Nothing. The game has no accounts, no ads, no analytics and no tracking, and it does not send any information to us or to any server we run.

Your player name

The name you type on the menu stays on your phone. If you create or join a Wi-Fi room, your name, team and in-game actions are sent directly to the other phones in that room over your local network or hotspot. Nothing is sent over the internet, and nothing is stored after the match.

Permissions

Network and Wi-Fi state, multicast: used only to host and find Wi-Fi rooms on your local network.
Vibration: short haptic feedback during play.
The game does not use your location, contacts, camera, microphone or files.

Updates

When installed from Google Play, the game asks Google Play whether a newer version is available so it can offer an in-app update. That check is handled by Google Play under Google's privacy policy.

Children

The game is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect information from anyone.

Changes

If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page with a new date.
